        <div id="sizing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Sizing by Room and Output
          </h2>

          <p>
            Coverage ratings are the least consistent number in the category. Vornado rates the Evap40 for up to 1,000 square feet, while Target lists it at 800 to 1,000. AIRCARE rates the MA0800 at 2,600 square feet for tight construction but only 1,700 for average construction, which is the more honest figure for most homes. Levoit's 3,000-square-foot rating for the Superior 6000S comes, by Levoit's own note, from a third-party lab test, and real results vary.
          </p>

          <p>
            A more useful way to compare is tank size and daily output. A 0.8-gallon tank like the Honeywell HEV320's is a single-room, single-night machine. Four gallons, like the Evap40, can carry a large room through a day. Six gallons, like the Superior 6000S, are for open-plan spaces where moisture leaks away into hallways and stairwells. If you are humidifying an open floor, buy more capacity than the rating suggests.
          </p>

