                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Maker or retailer runtime</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Honeywell HEV320</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">0.8 gal</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Medium room (no sq ft given)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 18 hr on low</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Levoit Superior Studio Smart</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">4.5 L (about 1.2 gal)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">600 sq ft</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 40 hr on low</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Venta AH530</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1.8 gal</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">485 sq ft</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Not stated</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Vornado Evap40</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">4 gal</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 1,000 sq ft</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 24 hr</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">AIRCARE MA0800</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">2.5 gal</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1,700-2,600 sq ft</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 36 hr</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Levoit Superior 6000S</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">6 gal</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 3,000 sq ft</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Up to 72 hr on low</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Room conditions matter as much as the machine. A drafty older house, high ceilings, an open staircase or a forced-air system that keeps moving air between rooms all raise the amount of moisture a humidifier has to supply. A bedroom with the door closed is the easiest case. Our guide to <a href="/what-size-humidifier-do-i-need/">what size humidifier you need</a> explains how to adjust for each.
          </p>

          <p>
            When in doubt, size up. An oversized evaporative unit simply runs on a lower fan speed and refills less often, and because its output tapers as the room gets humid, it is unlikely to over-humidify the space. An undersized one runs flat out, never reaches the target and goes through wicks faster. If you need a whole floor or more, a portable unit may be the wrong tool altogether, which the last section covers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="wick-costs" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Wick Replacement: The Real Running Cost
          </h2>

          <p>
            The purchase price of an evaporative humidifier is only part of what it costs. Over a few winters, the wicks can add up to more than the machine. Manufacturers give a replacement interval, and you should take it seriously, because a scaled, crusty wick evaporates less water and can start to smell. Here is what the makers say for each pick.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
