          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            An evaporative humidifier is the most forgiving way to add moisture to a room: no white dust from tap water, output that tapers as the room gets humid, and nothing to boil. You pay for that in fan noise and wicks, so the right pick is the one sized generously for your space with wicks you can buy every month or two.
          </p>
